  "query_preview": "..\n(Tonight through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1151 PM CDT Thu Sep 3 2026\n\nBottom line up front: Unseasonable heat will continue across the\nMidsouth for at least the next 10 days.\n\nGEFS and ECMWF ensembles continue to depict anomalously strong\nand persistent upper level ridging over the Midsouth through the\nnext 15 days. By this weekend, the upper ridge center will\nretrograde to the southern plains, placing the Midsouth under\nweak northerly flow aloft. A weak backdoor surface cold front\nwill pass through early Sunday. But without a backing cold\nairmass, this front is probably better referred to as a wind\nshift. 850mb temps will range from 22-25C, with surface\ntemperatures likely reaching 100F in several locations Sunday\nafternoon. The Heat Advisory has been extended through Sunday,\nbased on drybulb temps and the persistence of the heat.\n\nEnsemble model consensus continues to show the upper ridge center\nreturning east, likely settling over Ozarks by the middle of next\nweek. The effective ridge, or \"heat dome\",  will extend from the\n4-corners region, to the Carolinas. The main branch of the\nwesterlies will remain well to the north, from the northern\nRockies to the northern Great Lakes.\n\nAs in previous days, NBM continued to be 3-5 degrees to warm on\ndewpoints on Thursday. This morning's official dewpoint forecast\nwill be a 50/50 mix of CONShort and NBM deterministic out through\n12Z Sunday. In addition, minor downward adjustments were made to\novernight lows, to more closely match persistence in the\nrelatively drier air.",
